[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2956908743","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107061#issuecomment-2956908743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107061","id":2956908743,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wPtjH","user":{"login":"elzewyr","id":49611994,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjExOTk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49611994?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr","html_url":"https://github.com/elzewyr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-09T20:11:44Z","updated_at":"2025-06-09T20:11:44Z","body":"On its own, Jolt handles this scenario as intended, this must be a bug inherent to its integration in Godot.\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/25f5f041-7392-4ca1-81a1-0facb7a65a28)\n(here, cloth is paused during acceleration; does not disproportinately stretch at pinned points)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2956908743/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991955923","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107061#issuecomment-2991955923","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107061","id":2991955923,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yVZ_T","user":{"login":"elzewyr","id":49611994,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjExOTk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49611994?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr","html_url":"https://github.com/elzewyr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T15:03:26Z","updated_at":"2025-06-29T16:17:02Z","body":"In 4.5.beta1, with `physics_interpolation = false` it deforms in a different way, and more intensively.\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9b187866-7642-4fe6-a9e7-aff60b1901af)\n\nIt is worse with GodotPhysics3D, where it seems that only pinned points are affected by the movement. With `physics_interpolation = true`, both physics engines perform as originally described in the issue.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991955923/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3616695854","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107061#issuecomment-3616695854","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107061","id":3616695854,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XkmYu","user":{"login":"elzewyr","id":49611994,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjExOTk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49611994?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr","html_url":"https://github.com/elzewyr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elzewyr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T12:25:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-16T11:38:45Z","body":"I found out that the stretching is likely caused by a lag between the update of pinned vertices as part of `_draw_soft_mesh` in SoftBody3D, which is called on `frame_pre_draw`, and the PhysicsServer's `step`. Calling `_update_physics_server` inside physics process d8f7b1aa11e9ec99242ef24d300aeb566dcd58b1 causes a smaller stretching in the opposite direction, which is barely noticeable in GodotPhysics, but is more prominent in JoltPhysics.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3616695854/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]